# NestJS API

## Module layout

Organize by domain (`auth`, `users`, `roles`, `wards`, `surveys`, `imports`, `exports`, `reports`, `payments`, `refunds`, `settlements`, `files`, `audit`). Prefer Controller → Service → Repository (when useful) → DTO → Guard → Mapper.

Controllers stay thin. Business logic in services. No giant controllers/files.

## API shape

Versioned REST: `/api/v1/...`

Success:

```json
{ "success": true, "data": {}, "meta": {} }
```

Error:

```json
{
  "success": false,
  "error": { "code": "ERROR_CODE", "message": "Human readable" }
}
```

Never expose stack traces, raw DB errors, secrets, or internals in production responses.

## Validation

Validate body, query, params, files, headers. Backend validation is mandatory — never trust the frontend.

## Jobs

Long imports/exports/image work and reconciliation run asynchronously (`ImportJob` / `ExportJob` style). Do not block HTTP for huge workloads. Do not add a new queue framework without checking what already exists.

## Errors

Never swallow errors. Log appropriately; return safe messages. Frontend shows human-readable text only.
